---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy & boundaries — Meish"
  description="Trust is the product. No hidden use, no individual scoring, no sensitive data without consent. We work in English and Finnish."
>
  <section class="section container">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy &amp; boundaries</p>
    <h1>Trust is the product.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Meish only works if people trust it. We hold hard lines — not only because a regulation forces
      us to, but because breaking them would break what we sell: useful, human-centred work.
    </p>

    <h2>What Meish does not do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>No hidden use.</strong> People are never observed covertly for Meish work.</li>
      <li><strong>No staff surveillance.</strong> We never score, rank, or profile individual employees.</li>
      <li><strong>No individual scoring of guests or customers.</strong> We read patterns and situations, not people as targets.</li>
      <li><strong>No public shaming.</strong> Findings stay with the client organisation — never as internet content.</li>
      <li><strong>No sensitive data</strong> without a clear reason and explicit consent.</li>
      <li><strong>No promises made on a client’s behalf</strong> without their approval.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Example · guest signals (Clara)</h2>
    <p>
      In hospitality work, guests may share what helps their stay — parking, arrival, breakfast,
      accessibility, and how they would like to feel. Clara turns that into a staff-facing digest.
      Staff review and approve; Clara suggests, humans decide. That is one example of the same rule:
      tools support people; people keep control.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Consent is explicit and revocable.</li>
      <li>You can ask what we hold and have it removed.</li>
      <li>Contact: <a href="mailto:moona.m@meish.work">moona.m@meish.work</a></li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      <small>
        Draft for legal review — data controller / legal entity line, retention periods, and
        sub-processors to be confirmed before final publish.
      </small>
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
